5,"Embera Language and the Emberá Indian Tribe (Embera-Wounaan, Epena ...",https://www.native-languages.org/embera.htm,"Embera Indian Language (Emberá-Wounaan, Empera, Cholo, Pedea, Bedea) Embera is a Chocoan language of South America. Embera is spoken by around 80,000 people in Colombia and Panama. It has SOV word order. Sponsored Links Embera Language Resources Language map of Panama: Indigenous Northern Colombia: Maps showing the areas where the Embera dialects are spoken. Diccionario Embera: Online Spanish ...","Emberá, Northern",Chocoan
6,Music of the Indians of Panama: The Cuna (Tule) and Chocoe (Embera ...,https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_nrmE5mrRaEEz-uWhK6tX2ni4-TsW0odks,"Listen to Music of the Indians of Panama: The Cuna (Tule) and Chocoe (Embera) Tribes by Various Artists on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more.","Emberá, Northern",Chocoan
